Notebook[{
Cell["ArrayGraphics3D", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"1081d8ea-8bce-1d4c-b636-5856a8f8d532"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics3D", "[", "arr", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"d339b295-706d-8a44-b10c-c247a8a0594e"],
 " ",
 "draws the array arr as cubes arranged in space."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"5ecbbd27-779d-c945-b605-85dd7ac5df32"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics3D", "[", 
    RowBox[{"arr", ",", " ", "opts"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"0317e246-29e5-af44-88a5-ae647bc135d6"],
 " ",
 "draws it with the given options."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"9121a7e9-f587-f147-9042-b19917404dc9"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"d6575ed3-5e7b-5847-bb75-8ecacef4b8d1"],

Cell["\<\
An array of order one is drawn as a line of cubes, one of order two as a \
plane of them, and one of order three as a lattice. The entry at index tuple \
(i, j, k) sits at the point {i, j, k}, an index the array does not have \
standing at one.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"81d0b703-e10c-db44-8270-40bc47ba93d0"],

Cell["\<\
An array of higher order is drawn by tiling: the inner block of indices is \
drawn as a lattice, and the outer block repeats that lattice through space, \
shifted by its own extent and a gap. Everything ends up in one picture, since \
space has no room for pictures inset into pictures.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3df8198c-d0da-b64b-b0cc-01009909153b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is always a three-dimensional ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Graphics3D", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4a38f350-5ca1-4a47-aeae-249a7a285235"],
 ". For plane pictures at every order see ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayGraphics", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "11c5d6c2-0b82-af4a-b71d-f234a3742d4a"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"656da10b-dcd4-9746-a43b-5b6e2d3b3512"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Nesting\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"k1", ",", " ", "k2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}]}], "InlineCode"]],
   "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"4cdbc200-d7ce-2a47-ba31-c748938690a7"],
 " says how to split the indices: the blocks must sum to the order of the \
array and each must be one, two or three, space holding no more at a time. \
The default uses ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayNesting", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a2174c50-0d81-364a-a76b-2dc95c424bd9"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"84224466-ab5b-344b-bb05-843f68016fcd"],

Cell["\<\
The cubes have translucent faces and no outline, so that the entries behind \
them can still be read; an outline on every cube of a lattice reads as a mesh \
rather than as a set of cells.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6653ccc6-418b-6c41-b4a2-d025e583e422"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A gnomon in the near corner marks as many axes as the picture uses; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Gnomon\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"cf278dd7-a3ac-1844-9b4d-067928298b49"],
 " drops it. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Indices\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Colored\>\""}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3f1190b9-86bb-4945-bfe0-5cef47a28982"],
 " gives each axis a colour of its own."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5e021941-a8ca-b747-9a4a-d95da5bd4458"],

Cell["\<\
The reference implementation this package grew out of drew only the \
order-three case, and called such a picture a cubix; the name is not kept, \
but the look of it is.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f58e827a-0e5f-e540-bf01-23437e971fde"],

Cell["The other options are shared with ArrayGraphics.", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fdef882d-0d37-084b-b308-ab7d14d635c2"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"04983e25-7c93-704d-8db9-6bf963a2aeaf"],

Cell["At order one a line of cubes, at order two a plane of them:", \
"ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"8405d25a-8023-8240-9aef-98d0cae0e5e8"],

Cell["\<\
{ArrayGraphics3D[{1, 2, 3, 4}], ArrayGraphics3D[{{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}}]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"32909ee3-2998-c946-b903-e70dbadffee1"],

